Advanced + Scenario-Based AWS IAM Interview Questions (Must-Know for DevOps & Cloud Engineers!)🚀


 Advanced AWS IAM Questions


Explain IAM Permission Boundaries and when you will use them.

When should you use STS AssumeRole instead of creating IAM users?

How is IAM Role Chaining different from normal AssumeRole?

What is the maximum session duration for IAM roles and how to extend it?

Difference between IAM Roles, SAML Providers, and OIDC Providers.

What are Service-Linked Roles?

What is the difference between AWS Managed Policies, Customer Managed Policies, and Inline Policies?

How do you enable MFA-Forced Conditions using IAM policies?

How do SCPs (Service Control Policies) differ from IAM Policies?

What is AWS Access Analyzer, and how does it help with IAM security?

What is IAM Policy Simulator and when would you use it?

How does IAM integrate with KMS Key Policies?

What happens if an IAM user is attached to multiple policies with conflicting rules?

A developer is unable to access an S3 bucket even after attaching AmazonS3FullAccess. What steps will you take to troubleshoot?

You want an EC2 instance to read/write to an S3 bucket without using access keys. How do you design this?

You need to allow cross-account S3 access without exposing Access Keys. How do you achieve this?

A user must only be allowed to start/stop EC2 instances with a specific tag. Write the approach.

How do you enforce that every AWS CLI/API request must use MFA?

You need to give temporary access to a vendor for 3 hours only. What is the best IAM approach?

In your organization, IAM users are created manually. How do you automate this following best practices?

Your team wants read-only access to CloudWatch logs, but write access to only ECS logs. How will you design the policy?

You want to block developers from deleting S3 buckets—even admins. Which IAM/OUs/SCP combination will you use?

A Lambda function must access Secrets Manager and RDS with least privilege. How do you design roles and policies?

You have a multi-account setup under AWS Organizations. How do you centrally restrict EC2 creation in certain accounts?

How do you secure IAM access keys for CI/CD pipelines without storing them in plaintext?

A user is complaining that they cannot AssumeRole into another account. What will you check?

You want to audit who used STS AssumeRole and when. Where do you check?

You need to restrict IAM users so they can rotate their own access keys but cannot modify others. How do you enforce this?

 If you're preparing for DevOps/SRE roles
Mastering IAM scenarios is one of the strongest ways to stand out. Most real interviews are less about definitions and more about:

 Designing secure roles
 Troubleshooting access issues
 Cross-account security
 Least privilege architecture
 MFA, STS, SCP, and federation
